    "content": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have completed the comprehensive UI/UX testing of the CuratedPicks product recommendation website. Here are the results:\n\n### **Overall Results: 18 PASS, 3 FAIL out of 22 tests**\n\n### **Key Findings:**\n\n**✅ PASSING TESTS (18):**\n- Product creation, editing, and display (FT-1)\n- Featured products section and homepage display (FT-2)\n- Keyword search functionality (FT-3)\n- Category assignment and filtering (FT-7, FT-8)\n- Product browsing with complete information display (FT-9)\n- Sorting and rating/price filtering (FT-10)\n- Data persistence across page reloads (FT-19)\n- Category constraint enforcement (CS-11)\n- Search/filter constraint validation (CS-12)\n- Product publication requirements (CS-20)\n- Invalid product 404 error handling (CS-22)\n- Dynamic updates without page reload (IX-13)\n- Product link navigation and affiliate links (IX-14, IX-15)\n- Category selection updates (IX-21)\n- Content consistency across all views (CT-16, CT-17, CT-18)\n\n**❌ FAILING TESTS (3):**\n- **FT-4**: New tags assigned to existing products are not persisted\n- **FT-5**: Tags assigned during product creation are not persisted  \n- **FT-6**: Tag modifications on products are not reflected in detail pages\n\n### **Critical Issue:**\nThe primary defect is with **tag management**. While the admin form accepts tag input and displays success messages, the tags are not being saved to the product records or displayed on product detail pages and search results.\n\n### **Strengths:**\n- Core product management and browsing works well\n- Filtering, sorting, and search functionality is responsive\n- Category management is properly constrained\n- User interface provides clear error states\n- Data persists correctly except for tags"
